//    mathematically equivalent because each column j is independent, and within
//    a column we still process i in ascending order, so B[k][j] (k>i) is always
//    read before it is updated.
//  - Parallelize over columns j using OpenMP; each thread owns disjoint columns.
//  - Use a Noarr traverser with noarr::hoist<'j'> to make 'j' the outermost
//    dimension, then iterate columns via the traverser iterator.
//  - For each column, keep B[i][j] in a register and accumulate over k.
//  - Use state arithmetic for B[k][j] (reusing the per-column state) to avoid
//    rebuilding full states every inner iteration.
